 {:prediction
  "with INS6/INS7 in the mix every insert touches message/creationDate, so the ordered drive's per-attribute sorted cache misses on every following IC02/IC09/IS2",
  :measured-first
  "IC02 3.8 -> 33.8 ms served, IC09 7.4 -> 34.0, IS2 3.6 -> 30.3; the 17-op mix passed only 512 ops/s at 8 slots (1024 at 61.6% on-time)",
  :fix-1
  "datalog: the value order moves into datalog.index as a persistent sorted-set per attribute, carried across assert-quad/retract-quad with one conj/disj (ab4d7fb5); the drive cuts with subseq/rsubseq",
  :measured-second
  "WORSE: IC02 98.8, IC09 101.8, IS2 97.9 -- with one tracked version, a snapshot reader a few writes behind the head missed, rebuilt (into a sorted-set now, dearer than a vector sort) and untracked the head, so no later write could carry either",
  :fix-2
  "sixteen tracked versions per attribute (e75df8c2): readers find their version by identity, writers carry from any tracked version. Tests: two writes then a read with zero rebuilds; a retract the same; a reader five writes behind the head hits and does not untrack it (fails with one version). datalog 129/302/0; kotobase-peer on the pin 262/804/0"},
