  "INS1 -> IS1 shows the profile; INS6 -> IS4 shows the post's date; INS7 -> IS7 on the parent lists the comment; INS3 -> IC07 on the comment's creator lists the liker. IC07 is a top-20 window: a like whose date is older than every row of a FULL window was pushed out by later likes from the same stream -- counted as :outside-window, never as visible, never as lost."},
 :reading
 ["Six of the eight inserts served and interleaved with the eleven reads at 2536 ops/s on 8 slots and 3827 on 32 -- higher than the 13-op mix on the same hosts, with the ordering reads back at their read-only latencies after the engine learned to carry its value order across writes. 565 of 565 verifiable inserts visible; 9 pushed out of a full IC07 window by later likes; 155 unverifiable (dependencies outside the subset)."
  "The finding of the iteration is the second fix: a per-version cache must serve the versions its readers actually hold, and a read that rebuilds must not evict the head. Snapshot reads under a writer are the serving shape, and the first cache design was written for a frozen db."
  "Ratio to the audited No.1: 55 at 8 slots, 36 at 32 -- raw; still SF1 subset, no interleave by simulation time, no ACID suite."],
